course: dictionary
lesson: 7052
title: Pasta: a food and a dish
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pasta is a food made from flour, water and sometimes egg. It comes in shapes like spaghetti, macaroni and penne, and it is boiled before we eat it. Pasta is a noun, and it is uncountable: we say some pasta, not two pastas, when we mean the food.
explain: Read this sentence: «In Edinburgh, loud Oskar always answers for shy Filip: "He wants chips." Filip wanted pasta.» The words around pasta tell us that Filip is a child who wanted a meal, not a shape or a sauce. Context clues help you pick the right meaning.
explain: Pasta can also mean a dish made with pasta, such as a pasta bake. Look at «After sport the body needs to refuel and repair; carbs and some protein, such as a sandwich, pasta, yoghurt or milk, help recovery.» Here pasta is one of the foods that gives your body energy. Always check: does your meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Pasta is a food made from flour, water and sometimes egg.
fact: Pasta comes in many shapes, such as spaghetti, macaroni and penne.
fact: Pasta is a carbohydrate, so it gives your body energy.
fact: An adult should drain pasta, because boiling water and steam can burn.
fact: Pasta is a popular family meal in many English-speaking countries, and it came from Italy.
exercise: «Filip wanted pasta.» What is pasta? | A road in a town | A kind of sauce for bread | A jar with a lid | *A food made from flour and water, boiled before eating
exercise: What is pasta made from? | Sand and stones | Milk and sugar | *Flour, water and sometimes egg | Rice and salt
exercise: Why should an adult drain pasta when it is cooked? | To make it harder to eat | To make it sweeter | To keep it dry for a jar | *Boiling water and steam can burn
test: «After sport, a sandwich, pasta, yoghurt or a glass of milk helps recovery.» Which word names a food made from flour and water? | muscles | glass | sport | *pasta
test: The word pasta can also mean a dish. Which one is a pasta bake? | A cake made with sugar and eggs | *A dish made with pasta, baked and eaten warm | A loaf of bread | A bowl of soup
exam: Which of these is a shape of pasta? | *penne | bread | cheese | rice
